# ToolbarActions Patterns

## Action Types

Every action needs a unique `id`. Two variants:

- **`'icon'`** (default) -- Compact icon button with optional badge, tooltip, dropdown, highlight.
- **`'filled'`** -- Medium colored split button with text label. Main area fires `onClick`, chevron opens dropdown.

## Split Button (Filled Variant)

Must include `role="group"` and `aria-label` on `SplitButtonContainer`:

```tsx
<SplitButtonContainer
  role="group"
  aria-label={action.tooltip || action.label}
  variant={action.badgeVariant || 'default'}
>
  <SplitMainButton onClick={...}>{action.icon}{action.label}</SplitMainButton>
  {hasDropdown && <>
    <SplitDivider />
    <SplitChevronButton onClick={toggleDropdown}><FiChevronDown /></SplitChevronButton>
  </>}
</SplitButtonContainer>
```

## Dropdown Keys

Separator keys use array index (`key={`sep-${index}`}`), never `item.label` (separators have empty labels, causing duplicates).

```tsx
// GOOD
<DropdownSeparator key={`sep-${index}`} />

// BAD -- duplicate keys when multiple separators have empty labels
<DropdownSeparator key={`sep-${item.label}`} />
```

## Keyboard Navigation

Dropdowns support ArrowDown, ArrowUp, Enter, Escape. Track `focusedIndex` state and `actionableIndices` (memoized array of non-separator, non-disabled indices). Use `data-focused` attribute for visual state.

## Badge Variants

`badgeVariant` controls color for both badge dots/counts AND filled button backgrounds:

| Variant | Color | Hex |
|---------|-------|-----|
| `'default'` | Blue | `#4F46E5` |
| `'attention'` | Red | `#EF4444` |
| `'success'` | Green | `#22C55E` |

## Accessibility Checklist

- `role="toolbar"` on `ActionsContainer`
- `aria-label` on each action button (from `tooltip`)
- `role="menu"` on `ActionDropdown`
- `role="menuitem"` on `DropdownItem`
- `role="separator"` on `DropdownSeparator`
- `role="group"` + `aria-label` on `SplitButtonContainer`
- `data-focused` attribute for keyboard focus styling
